# White-Label

## Principle

All brand-specific values live in `~/shared/lib/brand`. Never hardcode "Workspace" in code.

## Usage

```typescript
import { brand } from "~/shared/lib/brand";

document.title = brand.appName;           // "Workspace" or "Acme Chat"
<img src={brand.logoUrl} />               // "/favicon.svg" or "/acme-logo.svg"
<span>{brand.copyright}</span>            // "© 2025 Workspace Team"
<a href={brand.supportUrl}>Help</a>       // "" or "https://support.acme.com"
```

## What Is Customizable

| Category | Env var | Default |
|----------|---------|---------|
| **Name** | `VITE_BRAND_APP_NAME` | Exordos Workspace |
| **Short name** | `VITE_BRAND_SHORT_NAME` | Workspace |
| **Description** | `VITE_BRAND_DESCRIPTION` | Corporate messenger |
| **Copyright** | `VITE_BRAND_COPYRIGHT` | © 2025 Workspace Team |
| **App ID** | `VITE_BRAND_APP_ID` | com.workspace.app |
| **Logo** | `VITE_BRAND_LOGO_URL` | /favicon.svg |
| **Accent color** | `VITE_BRAND_ACCENT_COLOR` | #FF8438 |
| **Theme color** | `VITE_BRAND_THEME_COLOR` | #1B1B1D |
| **Default palette** | `VITE_BRAND_DEFAULT_PALETTE` | orange-warm |
| **Default mode** | `VITE_BRAND_DEFAULT_THEME` | dark |
| **Support URL** | `VITE_BRAND_SUPPORT_URL` | (empty) |
| **Update server** | `VITE_BRAND_UPDATE_URL` | (default) |

## Creating a New Brand

1. Copy `.env.brand-example` → `.env.local` (or `.env.production.local`)
2. Fill in the `VITE_BRAND_*` values
3. Replace icons in `public/` (favicon, PWA icons, apple-touch-icon)
4. Replace icons in `packages/electron/resources/` (ico, icns, tray)
5. Build: `npm run build --workspace=web`

## Rules for AI Agent

- **DO NOT** hardcode "Workspace" in components — use `brand.appName`
- **DO NOT** hardcode copyright, URLs, descriptions — use `brand.*`
- **DO NOT** hardcode accent color — use theme tokens
- When adding a new brand-dependent value → add to `brand.ts` + `.env.example`
- `index.html` uses `%VITE_BRAND_*%` syntax — Vite substitutes at build time
